<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Arnotts says threat cost it A$10 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Arnotts says threat cost it A$10 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arnotts Ltd Chief Executive Chris Roberts said on Wednesday the company will have lost at least A$10 million from the extortion threat against the company's food products.</p>
<p>&quot;We estimate we have lost at least A$10 million after deducting insurance proceeds and taxed,&quot; Roberts told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;Our full loss will be known after further estimates are made,&quot; Robert said.  </p>
<p>Arnotts withdrew its products on February 14 after the company was embroiled in a extortion scandal involving a convicted murderer and police.</p>
<p>Shares in Arnotts, which is about 70 percent owned by Campbell Soup Co, closed five cents lower at A$8.85 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
